** OptiTap=C2=AE Compatible Flat Drop Cable for FTTH and Broadband Network=
s
------------------------------------------------------------

LYNN OptiTap Compatible Flat Drop Cables provide a straightforward option=
 for outside plant teams that need consistent mechanical performance in ti=
ght spaces. The singlemode OS2 design is available in toneable and non ton=
eable versions and supports standard OptiTap style architectures.


** Key Characteristics
------------------------------------------------------------

The ruggedized 3 mm core resists kinks and breakage during pulls and routi=
ng through ducts and enclosures.

The outer jacket removes cleanly while the 3 mm cable remains intact for p=
redictable connectorization.

Assemblies are built to order in the United States with short production l=
ead times.

An H style connector interface mates with OptiTap products from major vend=
ors.


** Performance Specifications
------------------------------------------------------------
Fiber Type            Singlemode Flat Drop=2C OS2
Insertion Loss        Typical 0.3 dB
Macro Bending Loss    Less than 0.75 dB at 1550 nm=2C 10 mm radius
Minimum Bend Radius   30 mm long term=2C 60 mm short term
Tensile Resistance    400 N long term=2C 1350 N short term
Operating Temperature -40 =C2=B0C to +70 =C2=B0C
LYNN OptiTap Flat Drop Diagram


** Construction Overview
------------------------------------------------------------

1.9 mm tight buffer fiber (G657A1) with aramid yarn inside an LSZH inner s=
heath.

FRP glass fiber strength members and optional bare copper toning conductor=
=2E

Polyethylene outer sheath supporting outdoor environments.


** Standards and Approvals
------------------------------------------------------------

ITU-T G.652.D=2C G.657A1 =C2=B7 EN 60811-1-1 =C2=B7 EN 60974-1-2-E1 =C2=B7=
 EN 60974-1-2-E3
